      heading: "What is the best long-lasting ED treatment?",
      body: `<p><strong>The best long-lasting ED treatment is tadalafil, which can stay active for up to about 36 hours - far longer than sildenafil's 4-6 hours - earning it the nickname "the weekend pill."</strong> If you want flexibility and spontaneity over a day or more, tadalafil is the clear choice.</p><p>Your long-duration options:</p><ul><li><strong>Tadalafil (generic Cialis):</strong> up to ~36 hours of active window from a single dose, so sex doesn't need precise timing.</li><li><strong>Low daily tadalafil:</strong> an even more seamless option - a small dose taken every day keeps a steady level present, so you're always ready without planning around a single dose.</li><li><strong>Compounded blends containing tadalafil</strong> (the 3-in-1 and 4-in-1 products) inherit its long-acting component, which is why some are marketed with "active up to 36 hours" framing.</li></ul><p>The trade-off with long duration is that side effects, if you get them, also last longer - but for most men tadalafil is well tolerated, and the flexibility is a major quality-of-life benefit for couples. If spontaneity matters more to you than dosing on demand, a tadalafil-based option is the best fit. Compare it against short-acting sildenafil in our <a href="/articles/sildenafil-vs-cialis">sildenafil vs Cialis</a> guide.</p>`,
