      heading: "What is the best ED treatment for men with heart conditions?",
      body: `<p><strong>For men with heart conditions, the best ED treatment must be chosen with a clinician - PDE5 inhibitors are safe for many stable heart patients but absolutely cannot be combined with nitrates.</strong> This is the situation where self-selecting a product is most dangerous and clinician involvement most essential.</p><p>The key considerations:</p><ul><li><strong>Nitrates are an absolute contraindication.</strong> If you take nitrates for angina or heart conditions (or use poppers), you cannot take PDE5 inhibitors - the combination can cause a life-threatening blood-pressure drop.</li><li><strong>Sex is exertion.</strong> For significant heart disease, a clinician considers whether your heart can safely handle sexual activity at all.</li><li><strong>Timing after a cardiac event.</strong> ED medication is typically avoided until you're stable after a recent heart attack or stroke.</li><li><strong>For many stable patients, PDE5 inhibitors are fine</strong> under medical guidance - plenty of men with well-controlled cardiovascular conditions use them safely.</li></ul><p>Because of all this, the "best" ED treatment for a man with a heart condition isn't a specific product you pick off a page - it's whatever a licensed clinician determines is safe after reviewing your full history and medications. This is precisely why every provider we recommend runs a detailed medical intake, and why unscreened "OTC" products are so hazardous for heart patients. Our <a href="/articles/ed-medication-side-effects">ED medication side effects</a> guide covers the nitrate rule in depth.</p>`,
