      heading: "What is the best ED treatment for occasional vs regular use?",
      body: `<p><strong>For occasional use, the best ED treatment is an on-demand generic or a per-dose option; for regular use, it's a low daily dose or a subscription that lowers your per-dose cost.</strong> Frequency is one of the biggest factors in what "best" means for you.</p><p><strong>If you use ED treatment occasionally</strong> (a few times a month or less):</p><ul><li>An <strong>on-demand generic</strong> (sildenafil or tadalafil taken when needed) is cheap and flexible.</li><li>A <strong>per-dose compounded option</strong> like <a href="/reviews/directmeds">DirectMax</a> gives you a stronger multi-mechanism dose without committing to a monthly plan.</li><li>You avoid paying for medication you won't use.</li></ul><p><strong>If you use ED treatment regularly</strong> (frequently, or want to be ready anytime):</p><ul><li><strong>Low daily tadalafil</strong> keeps a steady level present, so nothing needs timing - the most seamless option for frequent, spontaneous sex.</li><li>A <strong>monthly subscription</strong> can lower your per-dose cost and brings automatic refills.</li></ul><p>There's no prize for over-committing: if you're an occasional user, a subscription may mean paying for unused doses; if you're a frequent user, buying per-dose at full price may cost more than a plan. Estimate your real frequency honestly, then choose the model that fits it. A clinician can also help you pick between on-demand and daily dosing based on your lifestyle and how your body responds.</p>`,
